    answer: "Grafana, Sentry, and Datadog can all contribute to MCP operations, but they are not identical products. Grafana is often a flexible metrics, logs, and dashboard layer; Sentry is strong for application errors and traces; Datadog covers broad infrastructure and application observability. An MCP-aware server-boundary layer adds protocol, catalog, tool, client, and workflow semantics that generic systems may not capture automatically.",
    takeaway: "Choose the product that answers the boundary-specific question, then correlate it with the systems you already operate.",
